# {Label}

**Shows:** describe what the page shows. Main component: `{id}-page.js`; descriptor: `index.js`.

**Tabs:** none.

**Events:** emits none, listens to none.

**Slots:** declares none, contributes none.

**Uses from other pages:** none.

**Tests:** `tests/page/registry.test.mjs` (its descriptor).

## Adding a tab here

`python tools/retrodev new tab {id} <tab>` makes `page/pages/{id}/<tab>/index.js` (exporting `{{ id, label, Page }}`)
and lists it in `tabs: [...]` of `page/pages/{id}/index.js`. The shell draws the tab bar and remembers the chosen
tab (`app/page-view.js`); `Page({{ shell }})` gets the same `shell` as the page. Full steps:
`docs/dev/STUDIO-PAGES.md`, "Adding to the page".
